# {{ .Name }}

Kubernetes creates a "default" service account in each namespace. This is the service account that will be assigned by default to pods in the namespace.

The `kubernetes_default_service_account_v1` resource behaves differently from normal resources. The service account is created by a Kubernetes controller and Terraform "adopts" it into management. This resource should only be used once per namespace.

Destroying this resource deletes the adopted ServiceAccount, as it did before the Framework migration. Kubernetes can recreate a new default account with a different UID. Adoption does not mean that Terraform only forgets the account on destroy.

The `secret` and `image_pull_secret` blocks are authoritative after adoption. Include existing references that must be retained in the configuration. Adoption preserves omitted references initially, but a subsequent refresh and plan can propose removing them; this behavior also existed before the migration.

